2026-09-07 13:48:09 IST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:823 - nsflow: {"type": "AI", "text": "I have consulted the **CarFinanceAgent** to calculate the loan breakdown for your ₹12 lakh car purchase.\n\n### **Loan Summary**\n*   **Car Price:** ₹12,00,000\n*   **Down Payment:** ₹3,00,000\n*   **Loan Amount (Principal):** ₹9,00,000\n*   **Interest Rate:** 9% per annum\n*   **Loan Tenure:** 5 Years (60 months)\n\n### **Financial Breakdown**\n*   **Monthly EMI:** **₹18,682**\n*   **Total Interest Payable:** **₹2,20,920**\n*   **Total Amount Paid (Principal + Interest):** **₹11,20,920**\n\n---\n\n### **Important Considerations & Assumptions:**\n1.  **On-Road Costs:** This calculation is based on the **loan amount** of ₹9 lakh. Please remember that the \"Car Price\" of ₹12 lakh usually refers to the Ex-Showroom price. You will need to account for Registration (RTO), Insurance, and TCS, which could add another ₹1.5 to ₹2 lakh to the total cost. Most banks only fund up to 90-100% of the *Ex-Showroom* price, not the *On-Road* price.\n2.  **Processing Fees:** Most banks charge a processing fee ranging from **₹2,500 to 1% of the loan amount**. This is usually deducted upfront from the loan disbursement.\n3.  **Pre-payment Charges:** Since you are looking at a 5-year tenure, check if the bank allows part-payments or foreclosure without heavy penalties. This can help you save significantly on the ₹2.2 lakh interest if you have extra cash later.\n4.  **Credit Score:** The 9% interest rate is an estimate based on current market trends for used/new cars. If your credit score is below 750, the rate may be higher (10.5% - 13%), which would increase your EMI.\n\n**Would you like me to adjust the tenure to 3 or 7 years to see how it affects your monthly budget?**"}
